# FDD 21 review — "21 - Data Collection & Compliance - Roster of Employees" (Features
# 21.1-21.6). Ingested per abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/CONVENTIONS.md against the mied-v3
# Staffing graph (staffing-domain.ttl / staffing-permissions.ttl / staffing-api.ttl /
# staffing-sequences.ttl / staffing-technical-design.ttl), plus profpractice's own mied-v3
# conversion for the PPR-eligibility cross-domain check this FDD depends on. Per the
# CONVENTIONS.md dependency note, FDDs 10 (Staffing Administration), 18 (Roster of
# Positions), 22 (Employee Assignment Details), and 24 (Request for ID Collection) are
# concurrent, independently-reviewed sibling FDDs also expected to land in `staffing` —
# this pass does not see or reconcile against their output, only this FDD's own content.
#
# Source: "21 - Collection & Compliance - Employee Roster.docx" (.md sibling read first for
# the fast pass; docx unzipped for word/comments.xml, commentsExtended.xml/commentsIds.xml,
# document.xml — comment anchors resolved via commentRangeStart offsets against surrounding
# text, not just read in isolation — and word/media for wireframes).
#
# Structure used for the Requirement unit: the document's own "HIGH LEVEL SCENARIOS" table
# (20 rows) restates the Business Specifications prose at coarser grain and is SKIPPED per
# CONVENTIONS.md — every one of its rows maps onto an Addendum story below at finer grain.
# The Addendum's own Feature/story numbering (21.1.1-21.1.6, 21.2.1-21.2.5, 21.3.1-21.3.4,
# 21.4.1-21.4.5, 21.5.1-21.5.2, plus an unnumbered Feature 21.6 paragraph) is the primary
# Requirement unit used below — 23 items total (22 numbered stories + Feature 21.6's own
# unnumbered scope-pointer paragraph, modeled as Req_21_6).
#
# Comments (24 in comments.xml + 8 more reply-chain-only ids in commentsExtended.xml, 32
# total individual comment nodes): resolved/reply-only "To be confirmed"/"To be defined"
# placeholder comments (ids 11, 20, 21, 22, 24, 25, 1941181622 — verbiage/detail TBD on
# fields, warning text, and drawer content that already appear in the visible AC text) are
# folded into the relevant Requirement's own sd:notes rather than each becoming an
# Annotation. Comments with a real, still-live finding are modeled as standalone
# Annotations below: the unresolved "is 21.1.3 even a valid use case" contradiction (id 13,
# the single most significant finding of this pass — see Question_NewEmployeeWithoutIdContradiction
# and Req_21_1_3), the still-open "should there be an audit-log user story" thread (ids 6,
# 27, 330543191 — see Question_AuditLogUserStoryNotYetAdded), and the resolved-in-thread
# clarifications that materially changed the visible AC text (id 17/1926732478's PPR-status
# alignment with Epic 9, id 19/1327490318's Date-of-Hire chronological-order addition, id
# 15's "Add Assignment belongs to Epic 22" scoping, id 26/710379547's split-out of 21.5.2)
# are folded into their target Requirement's sd:notes as "already reflected in the visible
# text" rather than re-litigated as open Annotations. Tracked changes were not present in
# any meaningful volume in this document (a handful of formatting-only w:ins/w:del spans;
# nothing load-bearing found in a manual scan) and are not otherwise discussed.
#
# Wireframes: word/media has 30 images. The first 8 (image1.png-image8.png) are the
# document's own 5 captioned "Wireframe:"/"Wireframes:" call-outs (confirmed by viewing all
# 8, not assumed from document order — the "Employee Roster and Advanced Search" caption
# covers 2 images (list + advanced-search modal) and the "Quality Review"/"Collection
# Certification" captions together cover 4 (review screen, a confirm-run modal, a
# no-errors-found success state, and a certify confirmation modal)). The remaining 22
# (image9.png-image30.png) are uncaptioned, higher-fidelity Addendum screenshots in the
# same style as FDD 29's own addendum images; 8 were individually viewed (image9, 14, 20,
# 22, 26, 29, 30, plus image4 among the first 8) to confirm they are real product screens
# matching specific Addendum stories, not a distinct undocumented feature — including one
# (image29, extracted as addendum-f) that is directly load-bearing evidence for
# Req_21_4_1/21_4_2: its "Employees Not Appropriately Assigned"/"Employees with No
# Assignment"/etc. dashboard literally renders the placeholder text "Power BI Charts?" in
# the layout, showing the reporting mechanism for this feature was still an open design
# question at wireframe time, not settled UI. The remaining ~14 addendum images were not
# individually viewed; per CONVENTIONS.md's depth-calibration guidance, this is judged
# sufficient sampling across the document's span (employee list, demographic entry,
# confirmation, employment/assignments, collection landing, quality-review dashboard,
# employee-details drawer) to confirm the rest are the same application's screens for
# stories already covered above.
#
# Cross-domain corroboration worth calling out: staffing-domain.ttl's own
# Rule_CollectionRolloverCarriesForward and the CollectionOpenedEvent's
# carriedForwardCount/excludedCount payload fields are an exact, pre-existing match for
# this FDD's 21.3.2/21.3.3 rollover-inclusion/exclusion criteria — this FDD confirms rather
# than surfaces that rule. Likewise profpractice-domain.ttl's Rule_RosterEligibilityAssessment
# and Rule_ReviewedListedAbsoluteBlock (Reviewed-Listed hard block / Reviewed-Felony
# conditional-with-acknowledgment / active-review-status alert) are a near-verbatim match
# for 21.1.4's PPR acceptance criteria, down to the same named statuses — strong, positive
# cross-domain confirmation, not a gap.

